WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.370
Here's how to set up a controller in PadForge from the keyboard,

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.470
with NVDA reading along.

3
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.850
You're hearing a generated voice, and NVDA.

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:16.750
PadForge runs as administrator, so use the installed copy of NVDA.

5
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.930
A portable copy reads PadForge only when it runs as administrator too.

6
00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:26.195
On the Dashboard, Tab moves to Add Controller.

7
00:00:26.985 --> 00:00:31.595
Enter opens its list, and Enter again adds an Xbox 360 controller.

8
00:00:32.639 --> 00:00:34.913
NVDA: Profiles, data item, 2 of 4

9
00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:37.291
NVDA: Devices, data item, 3 of 4

10
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.841
NVDA: list Add Controller, data item, 1 of 1 Add Controller, button

11
00:00:42.006 --> 00:00:43.389
NVDA: Xbox, button

12
00:00:43.854 --> 00:00:46.073
NVDA: PadForge, window

13
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:49.693
Tab on to Devices, and press Enter.

14
00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.293
Tab through the list to your controller, and Space picks it.

15
00:00:54.084 --> 00:00:57.101
NVDA: Navigation Pane, toggle button, pressed

16
00:00:57.271 --> 00:01:00.288
NVDA: Full Screen, toggle button, not pressed

17
00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.679
NVDA: Devices, data item, 3 of 5

18
00:01:07.022 --> 00:01:09.170
NVDA: Slot 1, data item, 4 of 5

19
00:01:09.344 --> 00:01:15.090
NVDA: ALL, list DualSense Wireless Controller [Online], not selected, 1 of 15

20
00:01:15.256 --> 00:01:16.436
NVDA: selected

21
00:01:17.248 --> 00:01:21.898
Tab to the slot button marked 1, and Space assigns the pad to Slot 1.

22
00:01:22.779 --> 00:01:27.967
NVDA: list 1, data item, 1 of 1 1, toggle button, not pressed, Toggle assignment

23
00:01:28.132 --> 00:01:33.551
NVDA: pressed Assigned "DualSense Wireless Controller" to Virtual Controller 1.

24
00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:39.157
In the sidebar, Tab to Slot 1, and Enter opens its page.

25
00:01:39.847 --> 00:01:42.177
Then Tab to the Mappings tab, and press Space.

26
00:01:43.151 --> 00:01:45.300
NVDA: Slot 1, data item, 4 of 5

27
00:01:50.155 --> 00:01:52.970
NVDA: Mappings, radio button, not checked

28
00:01:58.672 --> 00:02:03.922
Tab reaches each row of the table, and NVDA reads its output and its source.

29
00:02:04.712 --> 00:02:08.182
Enter opens a row's settings, and Enter again folds them away.

30
00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:12.618
NVDA: Mappings, data grid A ← A, data item, 1 of 22

31
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.032
NVDA: B ← B, data item, 2 of 22

32
00:02:15.202 --> 00:02:17.435
NVDA: X ← X, data item, 3 of 22

33
00:02:17.619 --> 00:02:19.005
NVDA: selected

34
00:02:24.216 --> 00:02:27.266
On a row, the arrow keys and letters do nothing,

35
00:02:27.476 --> 00:02:30.486
so a key your keyboard maps never changes the table.

36
00:02:31.435 --> 00:02:32.485
NVDA: X

37
00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:40.427
Find more guides at padforge.org.
